                "Implement parasitic_free_publishing_account_serp_monopoly as useful distribution, not disposable-account spam or a promise to control search results. Publish the complete guide and interactive lite-tool on the owned domain first, then adapt supporting material for Medium, Substack, LinkedIn, GitHub Pages, Notion, and Gumroad Discover. Each permitted surface should solve a narrower problem and link clearly to the full tool. Set a canonical reference to the original only where the platform actually supports it; elsewhere use an original excerpt and source link rather than pretending a hyperlink is a canonical directive. Confirm public visibility, indexing eligibility, and platform publishing rules. Gumroad Discover exposure depends on marketplace eligibility and distribution, not merely creating a product listing. Record destination URLs and publication dates so updates can be propagated. Multiple useful search appearances are an acquisition objective, never an entitlement to Page-1 slots.",
